Fastify classifies **`GET`**, **`HEAD`**, and **`TRACE`** as bodyless by default.

This is defined in `fastify.js` around line 132:

```js
[kSupportedHTTPMethods]: {
  bodyless: new Set([
    // Standard
    'GET',
    'HEAD',
    'TRACE'
  ]),
  bodywith: new Set([
    // Standard
    'DELETE',
    'OPTIONS',
    // ...
  ]),
}
```

When a request comes in (`lib/handle-request.js`, line 29), Fastify checks `this[kSupportedHTTPMethods].bodyless.has(method)` — if the method is in that set, it skips body/content-type parsing entirely and goes straight to the handler.
